{% extends 'site/guideBase.html.twig' %}
{% block content %}
    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Getting Started</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>
                Welcome to Ultimate Warfare! This is a real-time multiplayer strategy game played entirely on an interactive world map.
                Your goal is to build a powerful empire by claiming regions, developing your economy, training military units, and conquering your enemies.
            </p>

            <b>How to begin:</b>
            <ol>
                <li>Join a world and choose a player name.</li>
                <li>You will be assigned a starting region on the world map with some basic buildings and units.</li>
                <li>From there, everything happens on the <a href="{{ url('Guide/World') }}">world map</a> &mdash; click on regions to build, send units, attack, and more.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </div>

    <br/>

    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Resources</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>
                Your resources are displayed at the top of the screen along with your income and upkeep per hour.
                There are four resources in the game:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <b>Cash:</b> The main currency. Used for constructing buildings, training units, and conducting research.
                    Generated by Economic Centers. Units have a cash upkeep cost &mdash; if you run out of cash, your units may desert you.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Food:</b> Required to sustain your military units. Generated by Farms.
                    If you run out of food, your units will start to die.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Wood:</b> A construction resource needed for buildings and training units. Generated by Woodcutters.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Steel:</b> A construction resource needed for buildings and training units. Generated by Iron Mines.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <br/>

    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Key Concepts</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <b>Regions:</b> Regions are the foundation of your empire. Each region provides building space (default 1000) where you can construct buildings and train units.
                    The more regions you control, the larger your empire can grow. You can buy unclaimed regions or capture them from other players.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>NetWorth:</b> A measure of how powerful your empire is, based on your buildings, units, and resources.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <br/>

    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Game Flow</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <ol>
                <li>Build economy buildings (Economic Centers, Farms, Iron Mines, Woodcutters) to generate resources.</li>
                <li>Construct special buildings (Barracks, Factories, Airfields, Harbors) to unlock military units.</li>
                <li>Research technologies to unlock advanced units and operations.</li>
                <li>Train military units and send them to reinforce your regions.</li>
                <li>Expand by buying unclaimed regions or attacking enemy regions.</li>
                <li>Join a <a href="{{ url('Guide/Federation') }}">Federation</a> to team up with other players.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
